{
  "id": "pain.008.001.08",
  "short": "pain.008",
  "name": "CustomerDirectDebitInitiation",
  "domain": "pain",
  "label": "Customer Direct Debit Initiation",
  "direction": "customer → bank",
  "mtEquivalent": ["MT104"],
  "related": ["pain.002", "pacs.003", "pain.007", "camt.053"],
  "summary": "A creditor instructing its bank to collect money from its customers' accounts under existing mandates. The pull counterpart of pain.001.",
  "whenUsed": "Subscription billing, utility collections, insurance premiums, loan repayments — any recurring collection where the payer has signed a mandate. The creditor's bank validates the file, replies with pain.002, and sends each collection onward as a pacs.003.",
  "gotchas": [
    "Mandate data is the whole game. A missing or stale MndtId, or a DtOfSgntr the debtor's bank disagrees with, produces a rejection now or an indemnity claim later.",
    "Sequence Type must track mandate history across files, which means persisting state between runs. Sending FRST twice, or RCUR before any FRST, both fail — and this state is exactly what gets lost in a system migration.",
    "SEPA imposes lead times: the collection date must be far enough ahead of submission for the scheme's advance notice. The required gap differs between CORE and B2B, so a file that works for one instrument can fail for the other."
  ],
  "fields": [
